// A labelled choice: the letter that names it, and the text it carries.
//
// Named `a_choice` so a field can be called `choice` — the singular names a
// list of records, the plural a list of strings, and a program's schema says
// which it takes at a glance.
//
// The label comes from the data, not from AutoCog — letter indexing is a
// property of the dataset, produced once when it is converted. A program that
// commits on the label (`repeat(choice.label)`) can only emit a label present
// in the record, so there is no letter it can produce that names nothing.

record a_choice {
  is {
    label is text<length=1>;
    value is text<length=40>;
  }
  annotate {
    label as "the letter naming this choice";
    value as "the text of this choice";
  }
}
